        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rl5" value="Application data (SAP etc.)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="90" y="820" width="380" height="36" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rv5" value="Out of scope, owned by those systems" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#605E5C;fontSize=11;fontColor=#605E5C;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="480" y="820" width="930" height="36" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zFlow" value="HOW TO READ THIS IN 60 SECONDS" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F7FAFD;strokeColor=#1F5B96;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F5B96;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="875" width="1420" height="215" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f0" value="1  Two active regions is a scale/locality decision, NOT a resilience decision - each serves its own population, neither stands ready for the other's failure." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="915" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f1" value="2  Cloud Cache redundancy and Azure Backup are genuinely different things, doing different jobs - this part built the backup half that was missing." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#107C10;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#107C10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="955" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f2" value="3  If East US 2 disappeared today, Chicago's users would have no path back - their data would survive in West Europe with nothing configured to serve them." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B77300;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#B77300;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="995" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3" value="4  The finance-first DR recommendation is conditional, not decided - it requires Northwind's own cost approval, exactly as Project 14's DR engagement required." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B77300;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#B77300;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1035" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="foot" value="Original architecture diagram for this capstone, not Microsoft's. Verified against terraform/capstone-northwind/avd-platform and Part H, August 2026. Self-contained, no remote icon dependency." style="text;fontSize=10;fontColor=#605E5C;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1105" width="1400" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
